infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Stateful session vs JWT: revocation versus local verification
  desc Same browser login — the chosen token decides whether you can terminate an active session now or only at exp
  compares
    - label Stateful session
      children
        - label Per request: ~1-2 ms store lookup
          desc KV/Redis p50; a Postgres sessions table costs 5-15 ms
        - label Revocation is instant — delete the row
          desc Effective on the very next request; logout-everywhere deletes all of a user's rows
        - label Rotation on login closes session fixation
          desc A token planted before login points to nothing after it
        - label Needs an external store on serverless
          desc Module-level memory causes probabilistic logouts across instances
    - label JWT (stateless)
      children
        - label Per request: ~0.05 ms local HMAC, zero IO
          desc Tens of microseconds of CPU — no store, no lookup
        - label No revocation until exp
          desc A per-request denylist just rebuilds the session store
        - label Window equals the access token TTL
          desc Honest hybrid: short 5-15 min access + a DB-checked refresh
        - label No shared store between issuer and verifier
          desc Wins at the CDN edge or across services that can't share state
theme
  palette #6366f1 #f43f5e
